{"kind":"request","text":"claude: add the browser security headers to the resident web UI — the P1 item from the 2026-08-11 security assessment that was wrongly lost in retirement churn: original 94e903f1 was retired as a \"stale self-request\" deferring to 0c2e43ec, and that entire implementing chain (0c2e43ec, e2879869/6f62c6bd, a075b03f/e8252c7c) is cancelled; the satisfied rows are only reviews of branch heads that never merged. Verified today: internal/service/ui.go sets only Cache-Control: no-store — no X-Frame-Options, no Content-Security-Policy anywhere in internal/service. Hugh authorized this revival today (2026-09-02) after a full review of the withdrawn backlog.\n\nTHE FEATURE. Every response the resident serves to a browser — the embedded UI pages and assets, and the JSON endpoints a browser can reach — carries the assessment's header policy: deny framing (Content-Security-Policy frame-ancestors 'none', with X-Frame-Options: DENY for older agents), a Content-Security-Policy for the UI restricting scripts and styles to the embedded bundle's own origin, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and a restrictive Referrer-Policy. State the policy in one place in internal/service so a future endpoint inherits it rather than remembering it.\n\nCONDITIONS: (1) tests assert each header on a UI page response, a static asset response, and a JSON view response, and fail if any header is dropped; the CSP does not break the embedded bundle (UI loads under the policy — verify against the served embed, not just unit tests). (2) Go gates green at the exact head; the embed itself is unchanged unless the CSP requires an asset adjustment, in which case make ui and commit the regenerated embed. (3) request/\u003cslug\u003e worktree with Rests-On this request; exact-head artifact for internal/service; independent review citing this request, original 94e903f1, and the 2026-08-11 security assessment; the review's Security conclusion must specifically confirm the frame-ancestors and CSP settings. (4) docs updated in the same head if any page states the resident's browser contract.","body":{"conditions":"Framing denied via CSP frame-ancestors 'none' plus X-Frame-Options DENY; UI-scoped Content-Security-Policy, X-Content-Type-Options nosniff, and restrictive Referrer-Policy applied from one place in internal/service to UI pages, assets, and browser-reachable JSON; tests assert each header on each response class and the UI verifiably loads under the policy; Go gates green at the exact head; exact-head artifact for internal/service published and independent review requested citing this request, original 94e903f1, and the 2026-08-11 security assessment with an explicit Security confirmation of the CSP; docs updated in the same head if they state the browser contract.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}